# Vue Admin Project - Agent Instructions

## Project Overview
This is a modern Vue 3 admin dashboard with TypeScript and comprehensive tooling.

## Tech Stack
- Vue 3 with Composition API and TypeScript
- Element Plus UI framework
- Pinia for state management with persistence
- Vue Router for navigation
- Vite for build tooling
- UnoCSS for atomic CSS
- ECharts for data visualization
- Axios for HTTP requests

## Key Features
- Auto-import for Vue APIs and components
- Development proxy for API calls (`/dev-api` -> `http://localhost:9999`)
- Responsive dashboard with user profile, data tables, and charts
- Role-based routing system
- Git hooks with Husky for code quality

## Project Structure
```
src/
├── api/          # API service modules
├── assets/       # Static assets
├── components/   # Reusable components
├── hooks/        # Custom hooks/composables
├── layout/       # Layout components
├── plugins/      # Plugin configurations
├── router/       # Route configuration (static + async routes)
├── stores/       # Pinia state stores
├── style/        # Global styles
├── utils/        # Utility functions and composables
├── views/        # Page components
│   ├── dashboard/    # Main dashboard with charts
│   ├── login/        # Login page
│   ├── register/     # Registration page
│   ├── role/         # Role management pages
│   └── ...           # Other feature pages
├── App.vue       # Root component
└── main.ts       # Application entry point
```

## Development Commands
- `pnpm dev` - Start development server
- `pnpm build` - Build for production
- `pnpm lint` - Run ESLint
- `pnpm lint:fix` - Fix ESLint issues
- `pnpm format` - Format code with Prettier
- `pnpm format:check` - Check code formatting
- `pnpm preview` - Preview production build

## Configuration Highlights
- Vite config with auto-imports and Element Plus integration
- Proxy setup for API calls in development
- Path alias: `@` points to `src/`
- GitHub Pages deployment path: `/vue-admin/`
- Auto-import directories: `src/composables/**`, `src/utils/**`
- Component auto-detection from `src/components` and `src/layout/components`

## Current Dashboard Features
The main dashboard (`src/views/dashboard/index.vue`) includes:
- User profile with avatar and login information
- Data table showing course purchase statistics
- Summary cards with financial metrics and icons
- Multiple ECharts visualizations:
  - Line chart for order trends
  - Bar chart for user activity
  - Pie chart for video data distribution

## Routing System
- Static routes: Dashboard, login, register, redirect
- Async routes: Documentation, Test, Guide, Role management, External links
- Layout-based routing with nested children
- Route metadata for icons, titles, and permissions

## Code Style Guidelines
- Use Composition API with `<script setup>`
- Follow TypeScript best practices
- Use SCSS for component-specific styles
- Leverage auto-imported Vue APIs
- Maintain consistent naming conventions
- Use Element Plus components for UI elements

## API Integration
- Axios configured for HTTP requests
- Global API proxy: `$api` available in components
- Base URL handling for different environments
- Mock data structure for dashboard charts

## Testing and Quality
- ESLint + Prettier for code quality
- Husky git hooks for pre-commit checks
- Lint-staged for optimized linting
- Commitlint for conventional commits

## Development Notes
- The project uses Chinese language in some UI text and comments
- Icons are from Ant Design icon set via Iconify
- UnoCSS is configured with presets for atomic styling
- State persistence is enabled for Pinia stores
- Component registration is automatic via unplugin
